<title>CHINA: China province sees record summer grain harvest.</title>
<headline>China province sees record summer grain harvest.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's biggest grain producing province of Sichuan is expected to harvest a record summer grain crop this year, the Xinhua Daily Telegraph said on Monday.</p>
<p>The newspaper did not give the size of the harvest.</p>
<p>It attributed the bumper harvest to favourable weather and increasing acreage under grain.</p>
<p>The acreage under grain in southwestern Sichuan reached about 2.28 million hectares this year, a rise of 51,000 hectares compared with last year, it said.</p>
<p>Of that total, the acreage under wheat rose by 42,000 hectares, it said but gave no further details.</p>
</text>
